# semgrep ignore rules for this repository.
#
# Each line below either excludes a path from scanning or suppresses a
# specific rule on a specific file. Format:
#
#   path/to/file                          # exclude entire file
#   rule-id:path/to/file                  # suppress one rule on one file

# install.sh: curl pipe to bash is the canonical OpenCode install invocation,
# identical to the pattern published on opencode.ai/install. The script is
# downloaded to a temp file first (not piped directly), which is the safer
# two-step approach. The remaining audit finding is informational only.
bash.curl.security.curl-pipe-bash.curl-pipe-bash:install.sh

# frontmatter.ts: the dynamic RegExp in extractFrontmatterField uses escapeRegex
# to sanitise the field argument before interpolation. The field value is always a
# hardcoded string literal at every call site ("id", "status", "updated_at").
# The nosemgrep annotation on the new RegExp line inside the file is the
# minimum-scope suppression; this entry is retained as a belt-and-suspenders guard.
javascript.lang.security.audit.detect-non-literal-regexp.detect-non-literal-regexp:opencode/plugins/lib/frontmatter.ts
